  "ja-consento": {
    "word": "コンセント",
    "url": "https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/%E3%82%B3%E3%83%B3%E3%82%BB%E3%83%B3%E3%83%88",
    "retrievedAt": "2026-11-10T12:29:06.776052+00:00",
    "revisionIds": ["92223608"],
    "language": "Japanese",
    "html": "<h2 id=\"Japanese\">Japanese</h2>\n\n<h3 id=\"Etymology\">Etymology</h3>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/Appendix:Glossary#clipping\" title=\"Appendix:Glossary\">Clipping</a> of <span class=\"Jpan\" lang=\"ja\">コンセントリックプラグ</span> <span class=\"mention-gloss-paren annotation-paren\">(</span><span class=\"tr\"><i>konsentorikku puragu</i></span><span class=\"mention-gloss-paren annotation-paren\">)</span>, <a href=\"/wiki/Appendix:Japanese_glossary#wasei_eigo\" title=\"Appendix:Japanese glossary\">wasei eigo</a> (<i class=\"Jpan mention\" lang=\"ja\"><a href=\"/wiki/%E5%92%8C%E8%A3%BD%E8%8B%B1%E8%AA%9E#Japanese\" title=\"和製英語\">和製英語</a></i>; <a href=\"/wiki/Appendix:Glossary#pseudo-loan\" title=\"Appendix:Glossary\">pseudo-anglicism</a>) derived from <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\"><a href=\"/wiki/concentric#English\" title=\"concentric\">concentric</a></i> +&#8206; <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\"><a href=\"/wiki/plug#English\" title=\"plug\">plug</a></i>,<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-KDJ&#95;1-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-KDJ-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-2\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-DJR&#95;3-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-DJR-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> used since the late <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meiji_period\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Meiji period\">Meiji period</a>.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-KDJ&#95;1-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-KDJ-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> Sometimes the source word is mistaken for the unrelated <span class=\"etyl\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/English_language\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:English language\">English</a></span> <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\"><a href=\"/wiki/consent#English\" title=\"consent\">consent</a></i>, which would be <a href=\"/wiki/transliterate\" title=\"transliterate\">transliterated</a> the same way.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Pronunciation\">Pronunciation</h3>\n",
